{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-78353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the center of the hyperbola $\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{16}-\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{4}=1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13988753/state.json" "file_sha256" "739794044d9cba07283d372cf877f44f7ecf6f3121537242ebdb455d3eda3a98"} {"question" "q-78353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $h=5$ and $k=1.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(5,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13988753/state.json" "file_sha256" "739794044d9cba07283d372cf877f44f7ecf6f3121537242ebdb455d3eda3a98"} {"question" "q-78353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13988753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ffd4734ecee11eae46a2ed4c95c42443f4b1ead9798dedc6e38d085c1b8ddf33"} {"question" "q-78353" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13988753/state.json" "file_sha256" "739794044d9cba07283d372cf877f44f7ecf6f3121537242ebdb455d3eda3a98"} {"question" "q-78353" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-5,-1)"] ["math" "(1,5)"] ["math" "(2,4)"] ["math" "(4,-2)"] ["math" "(5,1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13988753/state.json" "file_sha256" "739794044d9cba07283d372cf877f44f7ecf6f3121537242ebdb455d3eda3a98"} {"question" "q-78353" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(5,1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13988753/state.json" "file_sha256" "739794044d9cba07283d372cf877f44f7ecf6f3121537242ebdb455d3eda3a98"} {"question" "q-275272" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The center of the hyperbola $5{y}^{2}-2{x}^{2}-20y+4x=-8$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13988753/state.json" "file_sha256" "739794044d9cba07283d372cf877f44f7ecf6f3121537242ebdb455d3eda3a98"} {"question" "q-275272" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{y}^{2}-2{x}^{2}-20y+4x & =-8 \\\\ 5{y}^{2}-20y-2{x}^{2}+4x & =-8 \\\\ 5[{y}^{2}-4y]-2[{x}^{2}-2x] & =-8 \\\\ 5[(y-2)^{2}-4]-2[(x-1)^{2}-1] & =-8 \\\\ 5(y-2)^{2}-20-2(x-1)^{2}+2 & =-8 \\\\ 5(y-2)^{2}-2(x-1)^{2} & =-8+20-2 \\\\ 5(y-2)^{2}-2(x-1)^{2} & =10 \\\\ \\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{5} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,1,2\\,).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13988753/state.json" "file_sha256" "739794044d9cba07283d372cf877f44f7ecf6f3121537242ebdb455d3eda3a98"} {"question" "q-275272" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13988753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ffd4734ecee11eae46a2ed4c95c42443f4b1ead9798dedc6e38d085c1b8ddf33"} {"question" "q-275272" "f